    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1029">

                <pb facs="0991" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg893"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 244.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 280, of the 22d ultimo, and to confirm your telegrams of November 3 and 5,
                    and that <pb facs="0992" n="894" xml:id="pg894"/> of the Department of November
                    6, all in relation to protection to citizens of Cuba, Porto Rico, and the
                    Philippine Islands.</p>
                <p>The limit within which you may act is defined in the last paragraph of the
                    Department’s circular instruction of May 2, 1899, herewith enclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1029-a1.xml" xpointer="d1029-a1"/>
            </div>
